course: dictionary
lesson: 7168
title: Perky and the feel of a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone feels or how something looks. «Perky» is one of them. It means cheerful, lively and full of energy. A puppy that races around the garden, or a child who bounces into the kitchen, is perky.
explain: Read the words around «perky» to check. In the snowy wood, «robins perched and hopped on them in their perky conceited way». The robins are hopping about with energy, so perky suits them. The words «conceited» and «just as if they had done it themselves» tell you the robins look very pleased with themselves too.
explain: «Perky» can also describe a body part that stands up straight and looks bright, as in «perky ears». Think of a dog that hears a noise and lifts its ears. You can use the phrase «perk up» to mean becoming more cheerful, as in «After a nap, Sam perked up.»
fact: «Perky» means cheerful, lively and full of energy.
fact: «Perky ears» means ears that stand up straight and look bright.
fact: «Perk up» means to become more cheerful.
fact: The forms are perky, perkier and perkiest, for comparing two things and three or more things.
fact: Perky is a friendly everyday word; it is the opposite of droopy or glum.
exercise: «After a long rest, the puppy was perky again and wanted to play.» What does perky mean here? | Lost and afraid | Wet and muddy | *Cheerful and full of energy | Sleepy and sad
exercise: «Ella ate her toast and began to perk up.» What does perk up mean? | *Become more cheerful | Fall asleep | Go out of the house | Shout loudly
exercise: In «robins perched and hopped on them in their perky conceited way», what does conceited mean? | Very hungry | *Too proud of yourself | Afraid of the snow | Kind to others
test: Mum says the kitten has «perky ears». What does this mean? | Ears that are wet and drooping | *Ears that stand up straight and look bright | Ears hidden under its fur | Ears that are very big and soft
test: Of the three puppies, Biscuit is the ___ one of all. Which word fits the gap? | perky | perkier | perkily | *perkiest
exam: Jayden says perky means sad. Using the snowy wood sentence, why is he wrong? | *The robins hopping about with energy are lively, not sad | The sentence says the robins are asleep | Perky is a noun for snow | Robins are always grey, so they must be sad
